[SE00410] 🎭 OPERATOR IMPERSONATOR [Line 16]: '%' is not an operator you can overload.
  --> bad_oop.splat:16:5
    |
 16 |     fn op %(self, o::Child)::Child = self
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  Fix: Overloadable operators are: + - * / @ == != < > []

[SE00414] 🥚 UNHATCHED FIELD [Line 2]: field 'x' of 'A' has no default and 'init' never sets it.
  --> bad_oop.splat:2:5
   |
 2 |     x::i32
   |     ^^^^^^
  Fix: Give 'x' a default ('x::T = ...') or assign 'self.x = ...' in 'init'.

[SE00408] 🧬 GENETIC MISMATCH [Line 15]: 'go' overrides a parent method but has parameter types (txt) where the parent has (i32).
  --> bad_oop.splat:15:5
    |
 15 |     fn go(self, a::txt)::i32 = 1
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^^
  Fix: An override must keep the parent's parameter types and return a compatible type.

[SE00409] 👪 PARENTAL CONSENT [Line 12]: 'Base' cannot be born without arguments, so 'Child.init' has to introduce itself with 'super.init(...)'.
  --> bad_oop.splat:12:5
    |
 12 |     fn init(self):
    |     ^^^^^^^^^^^^^^...
  Fix: Call 'super.init(...)' with the arguments 'Base.init' needs, or give those parameters defaults.

[SE00101] 🔍 WHO DIS [Line 19]: 'A.nothing' has never been introduced to me. Did you invent it in a dream?
  --> bad_oop.splat:19:3
    |
 19 | r.nothing()
    |   ^^^^^^^
  Fix: Declare 'A.nothing' with ':=' or 'var' before using it, or check the spelling.

[SE00404] 🧊 ICE BREAKER [Line 20]: Tried to mutate 'r' in a read-only context. Some collections are immutable.
  --> bad_oop.splat:20:1
